% The work the default planner does on the chain of stats-semi-naive.dl.
% The recursive rule runs as its delta variant, which scans the paths the
% round before derived and looks up the edges leaving the node each ends at:
% the lookups read only matching tuples, so a path reads the one edge that
% extends it, or none at the end of the chain.  Every path is derived once,
% and the chain takes a round for each of its edges.  The query is answered
% from the whole fixed point, without the Magic rewrite, so that the counts
% are the program's.

edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).
edge(c, d).
edge(d, e).
edge(e, f).
edge(f, g).

path(X, Y) :- edge(X, Y).
path(X, Z) :- path(X, Y), edge(Y, Z).

path(a, X)?
